<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch NCM to shed jobs in Holland and U.K..</title>
<headline>Dutch NCM to shed jobs in Holland and U.K..</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch credit insurer NCM said on Thursday it would shed up to 225 jobs in the Netherlands and Britain, a spokesman said.</p>
<p>NCM said the restructuring was necessary as global competition grew fiercer and was made possible by the greater use of computers.</p>
<p>The restructuring, which will last until next year, involves the shedding of 125 of 700 jobs at NCM's head office in Amsterdam and 100 of 500 staff at its unit, NCM Credit Insurance Ltd in Cardiff. NCM employs a total of 1,300 people.</p>
<p>Last week NCM said it had posted a net profit of 13.8 million guilders in the first half of 1996 versus a loss of 5.9 million guilders in the same period of 1995.</p>
<p>- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000 fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
